 replace the live region in place. Game, player, and answer writes broadcast a
 small ActionCable refresh signal; connected screens immediately fetch their
-server-rendered live region. A JSON state endpoint is also polled roughly once
-per second as a fallback for browsers that lose the WebSocket connection. Both
+server-rendered live region. A JSON state endpoint is also polled every 300ms
+as a fallback for browsers that lose the WebSocket connection. Both
 the state endpoints and the ActionCable endpoint stay entirely in-process (the
 production cable adapter is `async`), so no external service is required.
 Player-facing state never includes option correctness until the moderator has
 closed the question; the player result view only reports `Correct!`, `Wrong!`,
 or `No answer`.
 
+## Scoring and prizes
+
+Every correct final answer is worth one point. Answers are timed on the server
+from `Game#question_opened_at` to the player's last selection, and the elapsed
+time is updated whenever the player changes their pick. The leaderboard orders
+players by points descending, then by the summed elapsed time of their correct
+answers ascending, then by join order as a deterministic final tie-breaker.
+
+The moderator and all phones subscribe to the same ActionCable game stream and
+fall back to frequent state polling, so question transitions and winner changes
+arrive together and promptly. During the game neither the big screen nor the
+phone result view reveals scores.
+
+Once the moderator presses `End quiz`, the big screen renders an ordered
+leaderboard and each phone renders the player's own place and points. The
+moderator can then:
+
+- Press the dynamically labelled `Top N` button to mark the first N positive
+  scorers as winners.
+- Press `Draw` to keep every player above the N-th-place score and randomly
+  award the remaining prizes among players tied at that score. Repeated clicks
+  redraw from a clean slate.
+- Press `Reset winners` to clear all winner marks.
+
+Zero-point players are never selected. Winner changes broadcast immediately and
+are reflected by the `Winner` badge on the big screen and `You won!` on the
+corresponding phones.
+
 The lobby QR code is generated locally with `rqrcode` and encodes exactly the
 same full join URL shown as plain text. No external QR or network service is
 used.
